# Day 12 — Python Dashboard and UART Integration

## Objective

Integrate the Python EV ADAS dashboard with STM32 UART telemetry and display real-time vehicle, ADAS, and fault information.

## Work Completed

* Connected Python dashboard to STM32 UART telemetry.
* Configured UART communication at 115200 baud.
* Parsed EV telemetry received from STM32.
* Displayed vehicle speed, battery SOC, torque and motor temperature.
* Displayed estimated range, accelerator and brake values.
* Displayed front, left and right ultrasonic distances.
* Displayed TTC and collision warning status.
* Displayed blind-spot detection status.
* Displayed alarm priority and fault status.
* Tested UART shell commands for system simulation and fault injection.

## UART Telemetry Format

```text
SPD:72.5 SOC:79.3 TRQ:75 TMP:27.1 RNG:2600 ACC:50 BRK:0
F:40 L:400 R:400 TTC:2.1s COL:1 BSD:00 ALM:2 FLT:04
```

## Testing Commands

```text
status
speed set 80
soc set 60
temp set 95
fault inject motor
fault inject soc
fault inject col
fault clear
obstacle 15
obstacle clear
```

## Result

The Python dashboard provides a real-time visualization layer for the STM32-based EV ADAS system and can receive telemetry through UART.
